// v62: Verified label cleanup — no literal $f score expressions; v61 item rules retained.
// v61: Hide low-value normal-tier set helms and worthless white/blue arrow/bolt quivers.
// Keep valuable set items, unique quivers, rare quivers and rare 2.5+ scoring unchanged.
// Sigon's Visor is ghm; identified and unidentified Great Helm sets are filtered.
// Covers low-value normal set helm bases and Dangoon's Teaching.
ItemDisplay[GROUND SET (ghm OR fhl OR bnh OR msk OR hlm OR skp OR cap OR 7ma)]:
// No plain or magic quiver bases, including 2-socket Heavy Bolts cqv2.
// Preserve rare, crafted, unique and set variants for their existing item rules.
ItemDisplay[GROUND (NMAG OR MAG) (aqv OR aqv2 OR aqv3 OR cqv OR cqv2 OR cqv3)]:
// v60: Repair literal rare-score expressions; stop rare/craft score overlays on unique rings.
// v59: Suppress conservative list of low-value noneth uniques at ground drop; preserve valuable/eth variants.
// Identified and unidentified drops use the same base code. No change to inventories.
ItemDisplay[GROUND UNI !ETH (7sm OR 7vo OR 8cb OR 8cs OR 8lb OR 8sw OR 9b9 OR 9fl OR 9kr OR 9sr OR gix OR kri OR lbb OR vbt OR xts OR xar)]:
// v58: Remove blue crafting-base equipment drops on the ground at ALL filter levels.
// No [LLD Craft] magic orbs, staves, wands, scepters, weapons, etc.
// Keep magic Diadems (ci3), Tiaras (ci2), small charms and magic jewels.
// Existing rare/crafted/unique/set items are NOT modified.
// Rule deliberately precedes inherited LLD craft show overrides.
ItemDisplay[GROUND MAG WEAPON]:
ItemDisplay[GROUND MAG (GLOVES OR BOOTS OR BELT OR rin)]:
// v57: Show blue Tiaras and Diadems; continue hiding other magic helms and amulets.
// v56: Hide all blue (magic) helm/circlet/amulet ground drops.
// Blue Diadems, Tiara, Coronets, circlets, class helms, and magic amulets are included.
// Filtering is GROUND only: picked-up items remain visible in inventory.
// Magic Tiara (ci2) and Diadem (ci3) are deliberately retained on ground.
ItemDisplay[GROUND MAG (ci2 OR ci3)]: %NAME%{%NAME%}
ItemDisplay[GROUND MAG (HELM OR CIRC OR amu) !(ci2 OR ci3)]:
// v55: Hide all magic and nonmagic gloves and boots on the ground.
// Gloves and boots cannot be socketed; no runeword base exception applies.
// Rare/set/unique/crafted boots and gloves keep their prior scoring/display rules.
// This terminal rule precedes all inherited visibility rules.
ItemDisplay[GROUND (GLOVES OR BOOTS) (MAG OR NMAG)]:
// v54: Strict ground-drop body armor and shield overhaul.
// No magic (blue) body armor or shields on ground.
// White/grey bases: only ethereal superior elite bases, with 0 or useful 3/4 sockets.
// Existing runewords, rare/set/unique/crafted items are not affected.
// Early terminal hides prevent later inherited rules from revealing junk.
ItemDisplay[GROUND MAG EQ2]:
ItemDisplay[GROUND MAG SHIELD]:
ItemDisplay[GROUND NMAG !RW EQ2 !(ETH SUP ELT DEF>=750 (SOCK=0 OR SOCK=3 OR SOCK=4))]:
ItemDisplay[GROUND NMAG !RW SHIELD !(ETH SUP ELT (SOCK=0 OR SOCK=3 OR SOCK=4))]:
// Explicitly retain qualifying bases ahead of later generic white/grey hide rules.
ItemDisplay[GROUND NMAG !RW EQ2 ETH SUP ELT DEF>=750 (SOCK=0 OR SOCK=3 OR SOCK=4)]: %NAME%{%NAME%}
ItemDisplay[GROUND NMAG !RW SHIELD ETH SUP ELT (SOCK=0 OR SOCK=3 OR SOCK=4)]: %NAME%{%NAME%}
// v53: Fix literal score placeholders and overly wide priority ground labels.
// v52: Targeted junk blue/white gear fix; rare helm scoring and blue jewels preserved.
// v53: Fix literal score placeholders and overly wide priority ground labels.
// v52: Targeted junk blue/white gear fix; rare helm scoring and blue jewels preserved.
// v51: Unique jewelry highlights; premium belts; helms ED+DS/CB+sockets+res; identified mauls scored normally.
// Hello Kitty-inspired pastel pink, white and bow-accented score labels.
// Based on v50 Tailored: identical visibility, 2.50 rare threshold, and item scoring.
// Rare names remain visually distinct from gold uniques. Decorations do not change drops.
// v50: Show unique belts; +2 Necro Summon/Sorc elemental circlets stronger; ID mauls require 2.5.
// v47: Identified rares require 2.50+ (special keeps intact); absolutely hide ground belts and rings.
// v46: Maul-family weapons are always visible (all six normal/exceptional/elite bases); preserve labels and score rules.
// v45: Corrected regular helm score floors (10-30% rolled ED, up to 20 CB OR DS). Hide set rings/amulets at all levels.
// v43: preserve qualifying identified rares on ground; valuable boots; specialist class/FCR and 180 ED score bumps
// v37: 3 glove foundations (skill/IAS/pierce, ED/CB/DS, FCR/kill), selective Glacial unique highlights
ItemDisplayFilterName[]: ÿc:Campaign
ItemDisplayFilterName[]: ÿc2Campaign-Strict
ItemDisplayFilterName[]: ÿc4Base
ItemDisplayFilterName[]: ÿc4Semi-Strict
ItemDisplayFilterName[]: ÿc9Strict
ItemDisplayFilterName[]: ÿc9Stricter
ItemDisplayFilterName[]: ÿc8Extremely Strict
ItemDisplayFilterName[]: ÿc8Extremely Strict+
ItemDisplayFilterName[]: ÿc1Hello Kitty - High Roller
ItemDisplayFilterName[]: ÿc13 Hello Kitty - Min Mapper
ItemDisplayFilterName[]: ÿc1No Items Out of Town
// Maul / Great Maul, War Club / Martel de Fer, Ogre Maul / Thunder Maul.
// v48: A rare weapon must be on the curated base whitelist BEFORE its score can show it.
// The numeric score is never a reason for a weak weapon BASE to bypass this check.
Alias[TAILORED_RARE_WEAPON_BASE_OK]: (TAILORED_BASE_AXES_SCYTHES OR TAILORED_BASE_MELEE OR TAILORED_BASE_THROWING OR TAILORED_BASE_BOWS OR TAILORED_BASE_CASTER OR TAILORED_BASE_ORBS OR TAILORED_BASE_ETH_ONLY OR leg OR hst OR msf)
// Exceptions requested previously: all mauls, 300+ ED identified rares, or 2+ T4 mods.
Alias[TAILORED_RARE_WEAPON_EXCEPTION]: ((TAILORED_ALWAYS_SHOW_MAUL !ID) OR (RARE ID (WEAPON OR 7cr2) EDAM>299) OR (RARE ID (WEAPON OR 7cr2) V15_T4_AT_LEAST_2_))
ItemDisplay[GROUND RARE (WEAPON OR 7cr2) !TAILORED_RARE_WEAPON_BASE_OK !TAILORED_RARE_WEAPON_EXCEPTION]:
Alias[TAILORED_ALWAYS_SHOW_MAUL]: (mau OR gma OR 9m9 OR 9gm OR 7m7 OR 7gm)
// v50: Unidentified rare mauls retained; identified rare mauls obey 2.50 threshold.
ItemDisplay[GROUND RARE !ID TAILORED_ALWAYS_SHOW_MAUL]: %NAME%%CONTINUE%{%NAME%}
// v47: Ground items only; never obscure inventory or equipped items. All rarities.
ItemDisplay[GROUND BELT !(UNI (zlb OR zvb OR ztb OR zhb OR ulc OR uvc OR umc OR utc OR uhc))]:
ItemDisplay[GROUND rin !UNI]:
// v51: More noticeable gold unique jewelry drops; preserve ID odds tooltips.
ItemDisplay[GROUND UNI (amu OR rin)]: %BORDER-9B%%MAP-9B%%DOT-9B%%GOLD%* %NAME% *%CONTINUE%{%NAME%}
// v52: Remove low-value ordinary blue and white dropped helms/weapons at strict tiers.
// White/grey premium bases and identified magic items remain subject to existing checks.
ItemDisplay[GROUND FILTLVL>2 MAG !ID HELM !CIRC !DRU !BAR]:
ItemDisplay[GROUND FILTLVL>2 MAG !ID WEAPON !SOR !STAFF !WAND !THROWING !SCEPTER]:
ItemDisplay[GROUND FILTLVL>2 NMAG !RW !SUP HELM !(SOCK>=3 MAXSOCKETS>=3)]:
ItemDisplay[GROUND FILTLVL>2 NMAG !RW !SUP WEAPON !(ETH OR (SOCK>=4 TAILORED_RARE_WEAPON_BASE_OK))]:
ItemDisplay[GROUND FILTLVL>2 NMAG !RW SUP HELM !TAILORED_SUPERIOR_BEST]:
ItemDisplay[GROUND FILTLVL>2 NMAG !RW SUP WEAPON !TAILORED_SUPERIOR_BEST]:
// v52: Remove low-value ordinary blue and white dropped helms/weapons at strict tiers.
// White/grey premium bases and identified magic items remain subject to existing checks.
ItemDisplay[GROUND FILTLVL>2 MAG !ID HELM !CIRC !DRU !BAR]:
ItemDisplay[GROUND FILTLVL>2 MAG !ID WEAPON !SOR !STAFF !WAND !THROWING !SCEPTER]:
ItemDisplay[GROUND FILTLVL>2 NMAG !RW !SUP HELM !(SOCK>=3 MAXSOCKETS>=3)]:
ItemDisplay[GROUND FILTLVL>2 NMAG !RW !SUP WEAPON !(ETH OR (SOCK>=4 TAILORED_RARE_WEAPON_BASE_OK))]:
ItemDisplay[GROUND FILTLVL>2 NMAG !RW SUP HELM !TAILORED_SUPERIOR_BEST]:
ItemDisplay[GROUND FILTLVL>2 NMAG !RW SUP WEAPON !TAILORED_SUPERIOR_BEST]:
// v49: HARD SCORE CUTOFF ON IDENTIFIED SCORABLE EQUIPMENT.
// Show only items scoring >= 2.50; item/affix-level and T4 bypasses do not override this hide.
// Do not apply to unidentifiable currencies, unique/set items or charms/jewels.
// Identified mauls are not exempt from the 2.50 score threshold.
Alias[TAILORED_V49_SCORED_EQUIPMENT]: ((WEAPON OR 7cr2 OR CHEST OR SHIELD OR HELM OR CIRC OR BAR OR DRU OR NEC OR DIN OR GLOVES OR BOOTS OR BELT OR QUIVER OR amu OR rin) !CHARM !jew)
ItemDisplay[GROUND FILTLVL>0 ID (RARE OR MAG OR CRAFT) TAILORED_V49_SCORED_EQUIPMENT FORMULARARECASTERHUNDREDTHS<250 FORMULARAREMELEEHUNDREDTHS<250]:
// Do not let ordinary/exceptional Glaives act like the valuable elite Ghost Glaive base.
ItemDisplay[GROUND (glv OR 9gl) (RARE OR MAG OR CRAFT) !(ID EDAM>299) !V15_T4_AT_LEAST_2_]:
// v45: Hide ALL set rings and amulets, identified or not, at every filter tier.
ItemDisplay[SET rin]:
ItemDisplay[SET amu]:
// v24: signature combo rating. These guaranteed score floors require ACTUAL sockets, never projected sockets.
ItemDisplay[RARE ID CHEST SOCK>3 EDAM>199 FILTLVL~1-10]: %NAME%%CONTINUE%{%CORAL%Signature combo: 4 sockets + %EDAM%%%TAN% Enhanced Damage%CL%%NAME%}
ItemDisplay[RARE ID CHEST SOCK>3 FCR>29 FILTLVL~1-10 (CLSK0>1 OR CLSK1>1 OR CLSK2>1 OR CLSK3>1 OR CLSK4>1 OR CLSK5>1 OR CLSK6>1)]: %NAME%%CONTINUE%{%TEAL%Signature combo: 4 sockets + 30 FCR + class skills%CL%%NAME%}
// Preserve these tooltip lines through the item-name rules below.
// Put known ED first on visible ground labels. Keep existing ground hide rules.
Alias[TAILORED_GROUND_ED]: (GROUND FILTLVL~1-10 (ID OR NMAG OR RW) ((WEAPON OR 7cr2) OR (TAILORED_ED_ARMOR EDAM>0)))
Alias[TAILORED_GROUND_ED_LABEL]: %YELLOW%%EDAM%%%GOLD% ED %WHITE%
Alias[TAILORED_ED_ARMOR]: (CHEST OR HELM OR CIRC OR DRU OR BAR)
ItemDisplay[(WEAPON OR 7cr2) (ID OR NMAG OR RW)]:%NAME%%CONTINUE%{%TAN%Enhanced Damage %WHITE%%EDAM%%%CL%%NAME%}
ItemDisplay[TAILORED_ED_ARMOR (ID OR NMAG OR RW) EDAM>0]:%NAME%%CONTINUE%{%TAN%Enhanced Damage %WHITE%%EDAM%%%CL%%NAME%}
